WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.668
This slide brings together the main organization

00:00:02.695 --> 00:00:05.539
tools from the module A function is

00:00:05.566 --> 00:00:09.145
best for one reusable task For example

00:00:09.316 --> 00:00:11.750
get profit can calculate profit whenever we

00:00:11.776 --> 00:00:14.961
provide sales and costs A module is

00:00:14.987 --> 00:00:16.697
best when we have a file containing

00:00:16.711 --> 00:00:21.000
related functions classes or constants For example

00:00:21.197 --> 00:00:23.303
metrics dot P Y could store several

00:00:23.329 --> 00:00:27.026
reusable business metrics A package is useful

00:00:27.053 --> 00:00:30.842
when several related modules belong together For

00:00:30.855 --> 00:00:33.658
example an analytics tools package might contain

00:00:33.684 --> 00:00:36.553
separate modules for finance health and reporting

00:00:37.487 --> 00:00:39.592
A class is useful when related data

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:43.250
and behavior belong together SalesReport is a

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.447
good example because it stores sales data

00:00:45.474 --> 00:00:47.908
and provides methods that summarize that data

00:00:48.842 --> 00:00:51.276
An object is one actual instance created

00:00:51.303 --> 00:00:54.750
from a class For example report equals

00:00:54.776 --> 00:00:57.053
SalesReport with a list of values creates

00:00:57.066 --> 00:01:00.961
one specific report object A useful progression

00:01:00.987 --> 00:01:04.632
for beginners is this Start with functions

00:01:05.539 --> 00:01:07.132
When a file becomes too long or

00:01:07.158 --> 00:01:10.132
contains several related helpers move related code

00:01:10.158 --> 00:01:13.382
into modules When you have several related

00:01:13.408 --> 00:01:17.237
modules consider a package Use classes when

00:01:17.263 --> 00:01:19.092
a concept has its own data and

00:01:19.118 --> 00:01:22.974
repeated behaviors Real projects may combine all

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.013
of these tools A package can contain

00:01:26.039 --> 00:01:29.842
several modules A module can contain functions

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:33.237
and classes A class can contain multiple

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:36.671
methods The structures work together rather than

00:01:36.697 --> 00:01:40.013
competing with one another The most important

00:01:40.026 --> 00:01:42.553
question is always the same which structure

00:01:42.579 --> 00:01:44.842
makes this project easier to understand and

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:45.513
maintain
